        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Fatal Conceit: The Errors of Socialism\n- People: Friedrich Hayek, William Warren Bartley\n- Topics: Socialism, classical liberalism, economics, political philosophy\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Hayek was born on 8 May 1899 in Austria-Hungary as Friedrich August von Hayek.\n- Friedrich Hayek was an Austrian-British economist and philosopher who was frequently referred to as F. A. Hayek.\n- Friedrich Hayek was best known for his defense of classical liberalism.\n- The Fatal Conceit: The Errors of Socialism is a 1988 non-fiction book written by Friedrich Hayek.\n- The Fatal Conceit: The Errors of Socialism was edited by William Warren Bartley.\n- Friedrich Hayek died on 23 March 1992.",
